======================================================================
SYNTHESIS
======================================================================

1. HYP-1981/THM-381 turns LRC into source reachability; THM-384
   reduces that source condition to the two observer-adjacent gaps.
2. In bounded exhaustive windows for n=3..6, every primitive speed set
   visits the closed LL source-gap fiber.  Initial segments are the
   extremal wall-only cases: open LL measure is 0 but wall LL points exist.
3. The naive integral proof route fails.  The conjecture
   integral(g_left+g_right) >= 2/n has explicit violations at n=5 and n=6.
4. The dynamic signal is exchange, not average size: gap changes are
   strongly anti-correlated in the tested windows, and LL appears as a
   bridge from one-sided-long LS into one-sided-long SL.
5. The inclusion-exclusion/pigeonhole identity is useful bookkeeping but
   tautological by itself: the overlap excess is exactly the LL measure.
6. Tournament Analysis on representative speed sets is transitive in this
   audit, ranking source-corridor abundance rather than exposing a cyclic
   obstruction.  That pushes the proof burden back to labelled endpoint
   pressure and compactified walk constraints.

